WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:17.792
"Ahh!" Katie and Joy screamed when the light went out.

2
00:00:17.812 --> 00:00:19.993
"Where's the flashlight?"

3
00:00:20.513 --> 00:00:21.113
asked Mom.

4
00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:22.954
But nobody heard her.

5
00:00:24.014 --> 00:00:27.335
The wind sounded like a train roaring over the house.

6
00:00:28.615 --> 00:00:30.616
They could hear it ripping through the trees.

7
00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:36.194
"Heads down," shouted Grandpa as the cellar door rattled.

8
00:00:36.214 --> 00:00:38.955
"Poor Jellybean!"

9
00:00:39.435 --> 00:00:40.176
cried Joy.

10
00:00:40.196 --> 00:00:42.817
"It must be so scary out there."

11
00:00:42.837 --> 00:00:46.738
"Magoo is scared too," said Katie.

12
00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:49.700
She could feel the dog shaking in her arms.

13
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:55.322
And then—whoosh!—the terrible sounds were gone.

14
00:00:56.002 --> 00:00:58.023
Outside, there was silence.

15
00:00:59.384 --> 00:01:02.150
Inside, everybody started to talk at once.

16
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.991
"Anybody hurt?"

17
00:01:04.411 --> 00:01:05.232
asked Grandpa.

18
00:01:05.252 --> 00:01:08.414
"That was some wind," said Dad.

19
00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.636
"What a tornado!"

20
00:01:11.116 --> 00:01:12.057
exclaimed Katie.

21
00:01:12.077 --> 00:01:13.838
"Is it over?"

22
00:01:14.398 --> 00:01:15.079
asked Joy.

23
00:01:15.099 --> 00:01:17.320
"We have to find Jellybean!"

24
00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.282
"Where's the flashlight?"

25
00:01:20.743 --> 00:01:21.723
Mom asked again.

26
00:01:22.844 --> 00:01:25.906
Katie found the flashlight in her box and switched it on.

27
00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:27.968
The beam lit up her face.

28
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.562
She swung the light and saw Mom, Dad, Grandpa, and Joy.

29
00:01:33.582 --> 00:01:37.405
"We're all okay, Captain," said Joy.

30
00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:42.587
The radio crackled, and Mom picked it up to fix the sound.

31
00:01:43.688 --> 00:01:45.069
"Listen," she said.

32
00:01:45.089 --> 00:01:49.991
"The severe weather in Boone County has passed," the announcer said.

33
00:01:50.011 --> 00:01:51.752
"We repeat.

34
00:01:52.152 --> 00:01:55.114
The National Weather Service has put out an ALL CLEAR.

35
00:01:56.154 --> 00:01:58.676
The tornado warning for Boone County has ended."

36
00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.801
"Look," said Joy.

37
00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:06.344
"Sunshine." Light glowed around the edges of the cellar door.

38
00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:10.646
Magoo slipped out of Katie's arms and ran up the steps.

39
00:02:10.666 --> 00:02:14.508
"Well, let's go see what happened," said Dad.

40
00:02:15.609 --> 00:02:18.090
He climbed the steps and pushed the door open.

41
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:21.152
"Come on, girls," said Mom.

42
00:02:22.713 --> 00:02:27.916
Outside, Katie and Joy saw a broken flowerpot and a twisted lawn chair.

43
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.301
A section of the garden fence was missing.

44
00:02:32.561 --> 00:02:35.602
Everywhere they looked, tree branches were on the ground.

45
00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.363
"The house didn't blow away!"

46
00:02:38.943 --> 00:02:39.603
said Katie.

47
00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:43.124
"That's good news," said Dad.

48
00:02:43.144 --> 00:02:45.504
"But there's a broken window in the spare room."

49
00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:48.945
Grandpa picked something up from the ground.

50
00:02:48.965 --> 00:02:52.606
"Here's one of my garden gloves," he said.

51
00:02:52.626 --> 00:02:56.207
"Let's go check the garden," said Mom.

52
00:02:56.227 --> 00:02:59.516
"And the chickens," said Joy.

53
00:03:00.657 --> 00:03:02.198
Katie and Joy ran ahead.

54
00:03:02.218 --> 00:03:05.039
"The lettuce is smashed!"

55
00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:06.259
called Katie.

56
00:03:06.279 --> 00:03:08.940
"The peas are in the mud!"

57
00:03:09.421 --> 00:03:11.622
called Joy as she ran along the fence.

58
00:03:11.642 --> 00:03:14.583
"Forget about the green beans!"

59
00:03:16.224 --> 00:03:20.185
Grandpa, Mom, and Dad caught up with the twins and looked at the garden.

60
00:03:20.205 --> 00:03:26.168
"I'm pretty sure my watermelon seeds got washed away," said Joy with a sigh.

61
00:03:27.636 --> 00:03:30.317
"We can get more seeds," said Grandpa.

62
00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:32.558
"There's nothing here we can't fix."

63
00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.719
"I hear the chickens!"

64
00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:35.859
said Joy.

65
00:03:35.879 --> 00:03:37.200
"I'm coming!"

66
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:39.701
she called as she ran to the coop.

67
00:03:40.801 --> 00:03:44.863
When she opened the door, the chickens hurried out, fussing and clucking.

68
00:03:46.104 --> 00:03:47.084
Joy looked around.

69
00:03:47.104 --> 00:03:50.986
"Everything looks okay here," she called.

70
00:03:51.006 --> 00:03:52.606
"Let's check the tree house!"

71
00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:56.428
She turned toward the pond and ran a few steps.

72
00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.500
"Oh no!"

73
00:03:59.121 --> 00:04:00.801
she cried, looking up the hill.

74
00:04:02.042 --> 00:04:03.743
She ran a few steps more.

75
00:04:03.763 --> 00:04:06.564
"Part of the tree house got crushed!"

76
00:04:07.744 --> 00:04:11.966
She suddenly remembered that Jellybean was still missing and gasped.

77
00:04:11.986 --> 00:04:15.027
"Poor cat," she murmured.

78
00:04:16.528 --> 00:04:18.429
"Let's go see," said Dad.

79
00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:22.110
He and Joy hurried to the tree house and climbed the steps.

80
00:04:23.211 --> 00:04:25.952
Dad cleared branches from the window and looked around.

81
00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.301
"I see some broken boards," he said.

82
00:04:29.321 --> 00:04:31.261
"But we can repair everything.

83
00:04:32.102 --> 00:04:34.782
All we need is a good set of tools and teamwork.

84
00:04:35.322 --> 00:04:35.943
Right, partner?"

85
00:04:35.963 --> 00:04:38.943
"Right!" Joy said.

86
00:04:40.104 --> 00:04:41.724
Then her eyes opened wide.

87
00:04:41.744 --> 00:04:43.245
"Did you hear that?"

88
00:04:43.265 --> 00:04:45.865
"What?" said Dad.

89
00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.246
"Listen," said Joy.

90
00:04:48.266 --> 00:04:54.528
MEEEOOOW! alive!"

91
00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:55.688
cried Joy.

92
00:04:57.148 --> 00:05:01.532
Dad got down on his knees and looked under a pile of branches and wood.

93
00:05:02.672 --> 00:05:06.275
He reached in and pulled out a wet gray cat.

94
00:05:07.496 --> 00:05:12.000
Joy scooped up the shivering Jellybean in her arms and leaned out the window.

95
00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.062
"All the Donovans are okay!"

96
00:05:15.462 --> 00:05:15.983
she said.

97
00:05:16.003 --> 00:05:22.728
"Five people, six chickens, one dog—and one great cat!"
